"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use an ordered index when you often ask for the entities whose property lies between two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, such as the ones whose health runs low, or visit entities in the order of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property, such as drawing them back to front:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let weak = world.spawn(Health(current: 2))","let weaker = world.spawn(Health(current: 1))","world.spawn(Health(current: 9))","world.index(ordered: \\Health.current)","","print(world.lookup(\\Health.current, in: ...3) == [weaker, weak])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered index is kept current the same way as an index by value ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/index(_:)-u1gw","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"):"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spawning, inserting, removing and despawning update it; a change in place leaves it out of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"date until the next "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/advanceChangeTick()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and until then "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/lookup(_:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/entities(sortedBy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" walk and sort the storage, so their answers are always current."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Keeping it costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for each insert, removal and despawn of an entity holding a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":", where an index by value costs O(1), so index a key path ordered only when you look it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"up by range or order. Indexing the same key path ordered twice keeps one index; a key path"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can have an ordered index and an index by value at once."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every key equals itself; a floating-point key isn’t NaN."}]}],"name":"Precondition"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" entities holding a "},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/index(ordered:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keeps the entities holding a component type sorted by a property of the component, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/lookup(_:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" finds the entities whose property falls in a range, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/entities(sortedBy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists them in order, without walking and sorting the type’s"},{"type":"text","t